and-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md\\n1:- [ ] T012 [P] In `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, insert one array item right after `'The answer holds for the rest of this session: do not ask this again on later turns.'`: `'For a new folder, start /speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete when the operator asked for the build itself: read that command document in full and follow it without :auto.'` (`$SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs`). Verify: `rg -c \\\"speckit:plan\\\" $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` prints 1, and `node --check $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` exits 0.\\n2:- [ ] T013 [P] In the standard next-steps block of `create.sh`, the one that prints `1. Fill out spec.md with requirements`, add after the lazy add-ons `if` block: `echo \\\"    6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan, or plan and build with /speckit:complete, unless one of them created this folder\\\"` (`$SSK/cli/spec/create.sh`). Verify: `bash -n $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` exits 0, and `rg -c \\\"6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan\\\" $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` prints 1.\\n3:- [ ] T014 Only if T002 shows the render map phase 005 generated in `$ADV/lib/render.ts` carries no `mutating` class per command string: in the deriver function that writes that map, add the class from the matching `commandPolicies` record, then run `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` (`$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` and its generated outputs). Verify: `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check` prints `fresh`, and the generated map in `render.ts` shows `read-only` for `/doctor:git setup` and `add-only` for `/doctor:speckit`.\\n4:- [ ] T015 In `$ADV/lib/render.ts`, add `childSession?: boolean` to `AdvisorBriefRenderOptions`, defaulting to `process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD === '1'`. When it is true, the command shown in the head line, and in an `Also:` line, renders `(parent-named only)` in place of its poli