a 300 s cap for chat runs and a 900 s cap for started-command runs. Verify: `node $R --print-argv claude` prints an argv that holds `-p` and `stream-json`, and `node $R --print-argv cursor` exits 2.\\n20:- [x] T012 In `R`, run each prompt with stdin from `/dev/null` and `AI_SESSION_CHILD` removed from the environment (operator approval of 2026-11-12), record `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --porcelain` before and after, restore each tracked path that changed during the run with `git checkout --` and delete each untracked path the run created, then append `{runtime, rowId, arm, locator, exit, changedPaths, restored}` to `--out`. Two guards protect work that is not the run's own. Before the first prompt, `R` exits 2 with `worktree_dirty` when `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --porcelain` lists any path outside this phase's `scratch/` folder, so a restore can never discard another worker's uncommitted edit. Before and after each prompt, `R` records `git -c core.fsmonitor=false rev-parse HEAD` and the output of `git -c core.fsmonitor=false stash list`, and when either changed it writes `headMoved: true` on the line, skips the restore and exits 3 without running another prompt. Verify: with one tracked file edited, `node $R --dry-run --runtime claude --row-id <first tune start id> --out $X/dry.jsonl` exits 2 and prints `worktree_dirty`. On a clean tree, `node $R --dry-run --runtime claude --row-id <first tune start id> --out $X/dry.jsonl` appends one line with `changedPaths` `[]`, and `rg -n \\\"AI_SESSION_CHILD\\\" $R` shows only the delete.\\n21:- [x] T013 In `R`, add `--set chat` and `--set g2`. `chat` reads `command-prompts.jsonl`, refuses with exit 2 any row whose `split` is `holdout` before reading its prompt, and picks by sorted id the first 8 `start`, 4 `run` and 4 `ask` tune plain rows and the first 8 must-not-start rows. `g2` holds six fixed prompts: a natural ask and a typed `:auto` command for each of `/deep:research`, `/deep:review` and `/speckit:complete`, the two deep loops capped at one iteration, all aimed at `$X/g2-fixture/`. Verify: `node $R --list chat | wc -l` prints 24, `node $R --list g2 | wc -l` prints 6, and `node $R --row-id <any holdout id>` exits 2 without printing prompt text.\\n22:- [x] T014 In `R`, capture the locator per runtime: Claude Code `session_id` from the stream, OpenCode `sessionID` from the events, Codex the thread id from `--json`, DSH the id the runner passes with `--session-id` and its `DSH_HOME`. Pi and Devin keep `UNKNOWN` until T022 records their locator source. Verify: `rg -n \\\"UNKNOWN\\\" $R` lists only the Pi and Devin rows.\\n23:- [x] T015 Create `T` with built sessions in the projected record shape, one per runtime, and cases for: 0, 1 and 2 `COMMAND:` lines, a document read before and after the first write, each policy with and without a write, a self-chosen `:auto`, a deep loop with and without `loop-lock.cjs acquire`, a refused `fanout-run.cjs` call, `/speckit:complete` with and without a spec folder first and a reader failure. Verify: in `$ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\\n24:- [x] T047 Create `A` with flags `--source <repo root>` and `--dest <dir>`. It exits 2 with `dest_exists` when `--dest` exists and with `dest_in_repo` when `git -C <parent of dest> rev-parse --show-toplevel` succeeds. Otherwise it runs `git clone --no-hardlinks <source> <dest>`, checks out the source's current commit as a detached HEAD, removes every remote from the clone, then copies from the source every directory named `dist` or `node_modules` and every `*.sqlite` file that sits under `.skilled/` and is ignored by git, to the same relative path, with `cp -Rc`. It never copies a dotenv file, meaning any file whose name starts with a dot followed by `env`. It prints one JSON line `{ok, dest, head, copied}`. Verify: with `D=\\\"$TMPDIR/arena-check-$$\\\"`, `node $A --source . --dest \\\"$D\\\"` prints `ok: true` with `head` equal to `git -c core.