{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794531774494,"sessionID":"ses_e2d9475e4ffeVXFuf4neYE7Ox0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d26dccb7002XTJing15RGRTfq","sessionID":"ses_e2d9475e4ffeVXFuf4neYE7Ox0","messageID":"msg_1d26da054001Qo2DSEunc7t4Sc","type":"tool","id":"call_0f0c514612be4d2d822d67d3","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build","pattern":"Plan the work with|Fill goal\\.md|create\\.sh","include":"*.md","limit":40},"output":"Found 12 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/plan.md:\n  Line 69: - **Loop without init**: on `/deep:research` or `/deep:review`, a write under the run's `research/` or `review/` folder, or a `fanout-run.cjs` call, before a `loop-lock.cjs acquire` call. On `/speckit:complete`, a write outside `specs/` before `create.sh` ran or a `spec.md` was written.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/tasks.md:\n  Line 79: - [x] T009 In `S`, add `loopInit(events, command)`. For `/deep:research` and `/deep:review` it is false when a write under a `research/` or `review/` folder, or a `fanout-run.cjs` call, comes before a `loop-lock.cjs acquire` call. For `/speckit:complete` it is false when a write outside `specs/` comes before `create.sh` or a `spec.md` write. It returns `null` when the run started no loop. Verify: `node -e \"import('./$S').then(m => console.log(typeof m.loopInit))\"` prints `function`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/spec.md:\n  Line 41: **Scope Boundary**: Instruction text and the generators and tests that keep it honest. One Gate 2 bullet in `AGENTS.md`, one generated pointer block in the Cursor rule, one bullet in each of the three hub routers, one line in the Gate 3 notice and in the `create.sh` next steps, the runtime table in the hook reference and a child-session downgrade in the brief renderer. Scoring, the recommendation schema and the brief head stay as phase 005 leaves them.\n\n  Line 212: - The Gate 3 notice is `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` in `spec-gate-core.mjs`, and `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` pins it byte for byte, so the notice edit and the test edit ship together. `create.sh` prints two next-steps blocks. The phased one already names `/speckit:plan`, the standard one names no command.\n\n  Line 227: - Name `/speckit:plan` and `/speckit:complete` in the Gate 3 mutation notice and the standard `create.sh` next steps (G3).\n\n  Line 254: | `SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` | Modify | One next-steps line in the standard block |\n\n  Line 286: | REQ-006 | `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` holds one line naming `/speckit:plan` and `/speckit:complete` for a new folder. `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` pins the new bytes and reports 0 failed. The standard `create.sh` next steps name both commands. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md:\n  Line 61: - **Gate 3 line** (`GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, `create.sh`): without it a plain build request gets the folder question and no workflow, because the advisor names no command for it (Measured Behavior).\n\n  Line 234: **Decision**: The notice and the standard `create.sh` next steps name `/speckit:plan`, or `/speckit:complete` when the operator asked for the build itself.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacin