ard `create.sh` next steps (G3).\n\n  Line 254: | `SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` | Modify | One next-steps line in the standard block |\n\n  Line 286: | REQ-006 | `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE` holds one line naming `/speckit:plan` and `/speckit:complete` for a new folder. `spec-gate-core.test.mjs` pins the new bytes and reports 0 failed. The standard `create.sh` next steps name both commands. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md:\n  Line 61: - **Gate 3 line** (`GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`, `create.sh`): without it a plain build request gets the folder question and no workflow, because the advisor names no command for it (Measured Behavior).\n\n  Line 234: **Decision**: The notice and the standard `create.sh` next steps name `/speckit:plan`, or `/speckit:complete` when the operator asked for the build itself.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/acceptance-criteria.md:\n  Line 59: | AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given the edited notice and `create.sh`, When the spec gate test runs, Then the pinned notice holds the `/speckit:plan` line and the test reports 0 failed, and the standard next steps name both commands | `(cd $SSK && node --test tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs)` prints `fail 0`, `rg -c \"speckit:plan\" $SSK/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs` prints 1, and `rg -c \"6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan\" $SSK/cli/spec/create.sh` prints 1 | Unmet | - |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md:\n  Line 34: - Wave 1, 12 tasks: T003 (`AGENTS.md`), T004 (`SYNC`), T005 (`HOOKDOC`), T006 (`advisor-runtime-value