{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794531782435,"sessionID":"ses_e2d9475e4ffeVXFuf4neYE7Ox0","part":{"partID":"prt_1d26dec62001bb7I3L34qRCNHg","sessionID":"ses_e2d9475e4ffeVXFuf4neYE7Ox0","messageID":"msg_1d26dd3ec001HcTN7ViwsBUKES","type":"tool","id":"call_d8c931355ecb419b96efb339","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md","offset":225,"limit":30},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md, lines 225-254\n225: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n226: - Drop the command from a child's brief, or send a child no brief: the operator chose the downgrade.\n227: \n228: ### ADR-006: The Gate 3 notice names the plan workflow for a new folder\n229: \n230: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"/speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete for a build (Recommended)\"\n231: \n232: **Context**: A plain build request gets no command from the advisor, so the first write meets the folder question and no workflow.\n233: \n234: **Decision**: The notice and the standard `create.sh` next steps name `/speckit:plan`, or `/speckit:complete` when the operator asked for the build itself.\n235: \n236: **Consequences**:\n237: - The pinned notice test changes in the same task wave.\n238: \n239: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n240: - `/speckit:plan` only, or both with no preference.\n241: \n242: ### ADR-007: `copilot` is removed from the runtime enum\n243: \n244: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Drop it\": \"The label is removed. Old stored records and any tool input carrying 'copilot' fail validation from then on.\"\n245: \n246: **Context**: No adapter or registration emits `copilot`, but the enum still lists it, so the hook index and the enum disagree.\n247: \n248: **Decision**: Remove the label with no retired list. A stored record carrying it is skipped by both metrics readers, a new diagnostic record carrying it is refused by `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, and tool input carrying it is rejected by `AdvisorValidateInputSchema`.\n249: \n250: **Consequences**:\n251: - Any old `copilot` record drops out of health and outcome summaries. None exists on this machine today.\n252: - A new test pins the skip and the rejection.\n253: \n254: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 255]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md, lines 225-254\n225: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n226: - Drop the command from a child's brief, or send a child no brief: the operator chose the downgrade.\n227: \n228: ### ADR-006: The Gate 3 notice names the plan workflow for a new folder\n229: \n230: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"/speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete for a build (Recommended)\"\n231: \n232: **Context**: A plain build request gets no command from the advisor, so the first write meets the folder question and no workflow.\n233: \n234: **Decision**: The notice and the standard `create.sh` next steps name `/speckit:plan`, or `/speckit:complete` when the operator asked for the build itself.\n235: \n236: **Consequences**:\n237: - The pinned notice test changes in the same task wave.\n238: \n239: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n240: - `/speckit:plan` only, or both with no preference.\n241: \n242: ### ADR-007: `copilot` is removed from the runtime enum\n243: \n244: **Status**: Accepted by the operator on 2026-11-12, \"Drop it\": \"The label is removed. Old stored records and any tool input carrying 'copilot' fail validation from then on.\"\n245: \n246: **Context**: No adapter or registration emits `copilot`, but the enum still lists it, so the hook index and the enum disagree.\n247: \n248: **Decision**: Remove the label with no retired list. A stored record carrying it is skipped by both metrics readers, a new diagnostic record carrying it is refused by `serializeAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, and tool input carrying it is rejected by `AdvisorValidateInputSchema`.\n249: \n250: **Consequences**:\n251: - Any old `copilot` record drops out of health and outcome summaries. None exists on this machine today.\n252: - A new test pins the skip and the rejection.\n253: \n254: **Alternatives Rejected**:\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 255]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/plan.md\",\"offset\":225,\"limit\":30}"},"time":{"start":1794531781730,"end":1794531782435}}}}
