{"type":"text","timestamp":1794531864948,"sessionID":"ses_e2d9475e4ffeVXFuf4neYE7Ox0","part":{"id":"prt_1d26f26df0027N7wdkouxIpVLr","sessionID":"ses_e2d9475e4ffeVXFuf4neYE7Ox0","messageID":"msg_1d26f19af001Afj73DJeILKdTo","type":"text","text":"Done. T013 implemented verbatim.\n\n**File changed**\n- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh` — one insertion, after the `WITH_LAZY_ADDONS` block in the standard next-steps block (line 2431):\n  ```sh\n  echo \"    6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan, or plan and build with /speckit:complete, unless one of them created this folder\"\n  ```\n\n**Verify output**\n```\nbash -n exit=0\n1\nrg exit=0\n```\n- `bash -n .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh` → exit 0\n- `rg -c \"6. Plan the work with /speckit:plan\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh` → `1`\n\n`git diff --stat` on the file shows `1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)`. No other file touched, checkbox not ticked.\n\n**One thing you should know (not changed)**\nThe `WITH_GOAL` block immediately after the insertion still prints `6. Fill goal.md...` / `6. Add goal.md...`, so the standard next-steps list now prints step `6` twice. I left it as-is because T013 names only the added line, and its Verify plus AC-006 count only that line. If you want the list renumbered, the two goal echoes need to become `7.` — a one-line follow-up task, not something I did here.\n\nNothing blocked.","time":{"start":1794531862239,"end":1794531864948}}}
